1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
One sky. Ancient China saw — a white
tiger.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Ancient China split the sky into four
animals, seven mansions each.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:20,000
The west meant the colour white and
autumn — so its animal is a white tiger.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Sima Qian wrote: "Shen is the White
Tiger." Its Belt is a balance beam.

5
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:34,000
The four outer stars: shoulders and
legs. The small triangle on top: its
head.

6
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Many scholars think the old character 參
drew these stars over a person. Later it
was borrowed for "three."

7
00:00:52,000 --> 00:01:00,000
The Bugis call it the Sign of Three;
Anuta, the Path of Three; Romania, the
Three Saints.

8
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:13,000
A grave in Henan, over 6,000 years old:
a dragon of shells on the east, a tiger
on the west.

9
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:21,000
In December, Orion rises in the east
during the evening and stands highest
after midnight.

10
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Arabia: the stars that brought the rain.

11
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:28,000
Follow for a new sky every week.

